# .vercelignore — trims what `vercel` (CLI) uploads as deployment source.
# Syntax is .gitignore-style, including `!` negation.
#
# Reasoning: the on-Vercel build (vercel.json -> tools/vercel-build.sh) needs
# exactly: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, rust-toolchain.toml, crates/**, web/**
# (sources, package.json, package-lock.json, .npmrc, .nvmrc, public/, scripts/),
# and tools/vercel-build.sh. Everything ignored below is provably outside that
# set. Do NOT add crates/ or web/scripts/ here — the wasm-pack build needs every
# workspace member's manifest and sources, and `npm run build` runs
# web/scripts/compile-docs.js first.

# Every pattern below is ANCHORED with a leading slash. gitignore semantics
# make an unanchored `docs/` match at ANY depth — the first deploy attempt
# removed web/src/docs/ (the Help-page sources compile-docs.js reads) exactly
# that way, and the build died in tsc on the missing ./docs/DocDiagrams.

# Rust build artifacts (multi-GB locally) — Vercel rebuilds from source.
/target/

# Stray wasm-pack output at the repo root, and the generated engine package:
# tools/vercel-build.sh regenerates web/src/wasm/pkg on every build.
/pkg/
/web/src/wasm/pkg/

# npm state — the installCommand runs `npm ci` on Vercel; a stale local dist
# must never mask a broken build.
/web/node_modules/
/web/dist/
/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
/web/stats.html

# Parity corpus + golden fixtures (~9 MB) — test-only. The property tables the
# engine embeds are copies under crates/frees-core/src/props/data/ (see
# CLAUDE.md), so nothing at build time reads fixtures/.
/fixtures/

# Java oracle tooling (needs a JDK and the ../frEES checkout — can never run on
# Vercel) and the local static-serve helper. tools/vercel-build.sh itself must
# stay in the upload: ignore the directory's contents, then negate the script.
/tools/*
!/tools/vercel-build.sh

# Repo meta not consumed by the build. /docs is the repo-root status/decision
# tree — NOT web/src/docs, which the build compiles into the Help page.
/docs/
/PLAN.md
/CLAUDE.md
/sonar-project.properties
